# Appium mobile suite conventions

- Framework code lives in `src/main/java`. Tests live in `src/test/java`. Env files, TestNG XML, and Log4j2 live in `src/test/resources`. Demo users and products are Java classes under `data/`.
- Screens do **not** extend `BaseTest`. Tests own TestNG lifecycle. Screens take the driver via `DriverManager` / constructor.
- Locators stay on screens as `private static final By`. No `PageFactory`, no Appium locators in tests.
- Runtime tests never call MCP. Appium MCP and filesystem MCP are authoring-time only (locator discovery, report dumps).
- Missing config → `ConfigException`. Secrets come from env / CI, never committed properties.
- Assisted heal only: propose locator/wait changes after review. Never silently rewrite tests on failure. Never auto-commit.
- No `Utils` / `GenericFunctions` classes. No Rest Assured, Excel/POI, or dual JSON libraries.
